  culture: `<p>Egyptians rarely give a flat “no” to a friend. Softeners are everywhere: <i>mish 3aarif ba2a</i> (“I don't really know”), <i>in shaa2 allaah</i>, <i>nshuuf</i> (“we'll see”). A direct <i>la2</i> can sound harsh; a <i>tsk</i> click with raised eyebrows means “no” too.</p>`,
