  culture: `<p>“Ten minutes” in Cairo is a figure of speech. Punctuality is flexible socially, less so in business. Voice notes on WhatsApp are the dominant way to communicate, and Egyptians send long ones, which makes listening practice easy to find: ask friends for voice notes instead of texts.</p>`,
